---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="simple">
      <h1>About</h1>

      <div class="me">
        <img src={url('/kokou.webp')} width="112" height="112" alt="Kokou Egbewatt" decoding="async" />
        <div>
          <div class="name">Kokou Egbewatt</div>
          <div class="role">Senior DevOps and Platform Engineer</div>
          <div class="links">
            <a href="mailto:kokou.egbewatt@gmail.com">email</a>
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kinfinity3/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">linkedin</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/kokou-egbewatt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>These days I mostly work on data and ML infrastructure: bare-metal and EKS GPU clusters, high-throughput model serving pipelines, and the eBPF/DCGM observability that tells you exactly which node is melting down.</p>
      <p>My local lab runs on an RTX 5060 with 8 GB, a six-core Ryzen, and WSL2. We would be profiling and benchmarking on local hardware over waiting on cloud quota approvals, especially since the mechanics scale directly. Memory pressure, KV-cache sizing, scheduler behavior, and NVIDIA DRA semantics follow the same core engineering principles whether you hit limits at batch 4 on a single workstation or batch 128 across multi-node clusters.</p>
      <p>Most of what I write here comes out of <a href="https://github.com/kokou-egbewatt/NeuroMesh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NeuroMesh</a>, the AI runtime I'm building, and <a href="https://github.com/kokou-egbewatt/infinity-bench" target="_blank" rel="noopener">infinity-bench</a>, which holds this site and the harnesses behind its numbers.</p>
      <p>Core stack: Kubernetes (EKS in production, k3s locally), NVIDIA GPU Operator, Kueue, vLLM, and llama.cpp. I use Ray for distributed workloads, Terraform and Argo CD for immutable GitOps pipelines, and Prometheus with eBPF for deep runtime tracing. Python and Go for custom controllers and automation glue.</p>
      <p>If something I published is wrong, <a href="mailto:kokou.egbewatt@gmail.com">email me</a>. I'll fix it and credit you on the <a href={url('/corrections')}>Corrections</a> page.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .me {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 18px;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
  }
  .me img {
    width: 112px;
    height: 112px;
    flex: none;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .name {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 21px;
    color: var(--hi);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .role {
    color: var(--tx2);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    margin: 2px 0 8px;
  }
  .links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
  }
  .links a {
    color: var(--tx3);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--line2);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .links a:hover {
    color: var(--tx);
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .me img {
      width: 88px;
      height: 88px;
    }
  }
</style>
